# Opaque wrapper of the program's `malloc_message` hook, a function pointer.
Hook	function pointer	Kani
# The C caller hands over the block it frees under the entry point's contract.
axiom_c_call	C-program contract	none (assumption)
# The two volatile reads of the hook slots the C program writes.
message_hook	UnsafeCell/volatile/transmute	Kani	trusted (partly checked, Kani: api::jemalloc::kani_hook::message_hook_picks_first_set; not checked: that the C program stores only null or a function in the two hook slots, and never while the volatile reads run, which is its contract)
